    {
      "id": "california-governor-askca-release",
      "url": "https://www.gov.ca.gov/2026/09/09/government-made-easier-governor-newsom-introduces-askca-a-new-ai-powered-tool-for-californians/",
      "authority": "Primary California announcement for the September 9 pilot invitation, intended service-navigation scope, builder and separate CalCareers plan.",
      "passages": [
        "California has developed AskCA, a new AI-powered tool to help Californians better connect with state services through a streamlined model designed around life events like finding a job, starting a business, or recovering from a disaster. The state is now seeking volunteers to help test and refine this new tool.",
        "Starting today, Californians can sign up to be part of the pilot.",
        "Testers must be 18 years or older and a California resident.",
        "The prototype was built by the Office of Data and Innovation to navigate people through life events including, for example:",
        "The California Office of Data and Innovation built AskCA’s knowledge base in collaboration with Anthropic’s Claude model, with security support from the California Department of Technology.",
        "CalHR is the first department to deploy the AskCA prototype in a live public service, powering a new AI‑driven job‑skills‑matching feature launching September 30 on CalCareers.ca.gov."
      ],
      "limitation": "Government announcement and planned dates; company/state descriptions are not independent accuracy, uptake or service-outcome evidence.",
      "fullSource": {
        "path": "operations/product-stewards/newsstand/candidates/askca-pilot-20260911/source/governor-release.txt",
        "sha256": "38e91ba7b1cbf0226f4a8fa35c7bf396e170c9f96b1d5dcca9eb2a6e6b174471"
      },
      "original": {
        "path": "operations/product-stewards/newsstand/candidates/askca-pilot-20260911/source/governor-release.html",
        "sha256": "30fdec885bd9e8616247c6ec17daab353572c7b5b56754b3c70a030e0b11c10e"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "askca-pilot-page",
      "url": "https://ask.ca.gov/",
      "authority": "Current official pilot page for who may participate and when the hands-on test occurs.",
      "passages": [
        "California is making a digital assistant to help people find and navigate state services. We want your help to make it the best it can be.",
        "Be 18 years or older",
        "Live in California",
        "In October, you can explore the digital assistant on your own. You will be able to chat with the AI and rate responses. You’ll get surveys to share your experience."
      ],
      "limitation": "Pilot recruitment page, not proof the assistant is generally available or effective.",
      "fullSource": {
        "path": "operations/product-stewards/newsstand/candidates/askca-pilot-20260911/source/askca-pilot.txt",
        "sha256": "c8e6ba7223201d5ec8e1a3655d19888d5b9cd9a82093e66e343d79e06821b630"
      },
      "original": {
        "path": "operations/product-stewards/newsstand/candidates/askca-pilot-20260911/source/askca-pilot.html",
        "sha256": "b13d2de6f00f72d4fd2147959ca518da4d201cd48c556c70c16ecd60e66bd06f"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "askca-about",
      "url": "https://ask.ca.gov/about",
      "authority": "Current official product description for the intended life-event interaction, source search, prototype status and admitted accuracy limit.",
      "passages": [
        "This is a prototype. By signing up for the pilot testing, your feedback will help us improve it. It may not always get things right — every question you ask helps us make it better.",
        "We're making it easier. Tell us what you're going through — whether that's finding a state job, recovering from a disaster, or having a child — and we'll help you find the right programs, services, and next steps.",
        "No government jargon. No personal information. Just tell us what you're dealing with.",
        "We pull from state, federal, and county sources in real time to find accurate answers.",
        "We give you clear next steps and direct links. You spend less time searching.",
        "We do NOT train the model based on your conversations.",
        "Our team reviews conversations to find gaps and catch errors."
      ],
      "limitation": "State description of intended design and practices; words such as accurate and trusted are not an independent performance guarantee.",
      "fullSource": {
        "path": "operations/product-stewards/newsstand/candidates/askca-pilot-20260911/source/askca-about.txt",
        "sha256": "3bc1519418e6062687746ae56c76a60e86e59067c71967939e5c7fa3ed211a68"
      },
      "original": {
        "path": "operations/product-stewards/newsstand/candidates/askca-pilot-20260911/source/askca-about.html",
        "sha256": "ea57fed18bf915b665d567f219b8b861e4de4b2eb1b3f4359d6d91250c85ba63"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "askca-conditions",
      "url": "https://ask.ca.gov/conditions-of-use",
      "authority": "Current official conditions for accuracy, sensitive information and checking material answers.",
      "passages": [
        "ODI values, but does not guarantee, the accuracy of content on AskCA.",
        "The AI can make mistakes. It might give you information that is wrong, out of date, or not right for your specific situation. Always double-check important info with the actual state agency.",
        "Since this is an AI, please do not type in sensitive details including your Social Security number or private health information.",
        "We may use information you send us to improve our services or to respond to you.",
        "We may forward your information to other state employees who may be better able to help you."
      ],
      "limitation": "Terms state current rules and disclaimers; they do not measure how often errors occur or resolve every privacy scenario.",
      "fullSource": {
        "path": "operations/product-stewards/newsstand/candidates/askca-pilot-20260911/source/askca-conditions.txt",
        "sha256": "6e5f5dbc0a5c2c5923e79d65e2045d2ef7cfb38661940abaa9e27d8d97241bf9"
      },
